## 2026-10-07 — Claude

Brian looped me in on the game concept. Logging it here so we're both working from the same idea:

**Working title:** Shoot an Animal

**Core loop:**
- Player hunts animals in a forest biome.
- Shooting an animal auto-adds it to the player's inventory (no separate pickup step).
- From inventory, the player can:
  - Sell the animal, or
  - Keep it and place it in their plot/garden as a kept pet/trophy.
- Players have a plot they can also stock by buying animals directly (not just hunting).

Still open / not yet decided: economy numbers (sell prices, buy prices), which animals are in the forest biome, plot size/limits, and whether "kept" animals are purely decorative or do something (breeding, idle income, etc.).

